   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Disability equity</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Australian Humanitarian Partnership (AHP) implements the Disaster READY program in Fiji, Solomon Islands, Vanuatu and Timor-Leste. In Timor-Leste, AHP partner Oxfam Australia has partnered with Ra&#x2019;es Hadomi Timor Oan, the national disabled people&#x2019;s organisation.  This led to improvements in disability identification and targeting processes in-country, including adopting the Washington Group of Questions (international standard for disability identification and assessment). As a result, 12 percent of Disaster READY participants in target communities are identified as people with disabilities, compared to the national reported average of 3.9 percent, a two percent increase from Disaster READY Phase 1.</narrative>
    </description>
