    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Australian Humanitarian Partnership implements a Disaster READY program in Fiji, Solomon Islands, Vanuatu and Timor-Leste. In Fiji, AHP partner Oxfam Australia supported 17 rural fisher women from eight communities across Rewa, Tailevu and Ra provinces to participate in a training of trainers workshop to strengthen resilience and encourage disaster risk reduction approaches to their livelihoods. Climate change adaptation activities included identifying local adaptation knowledge and mitigation activities to incorporate into community level disaster preparedness and response approaches, strengthening resilience.</narrative>
